# A deploy is announced in a Slack channel.
#
# A deployment is named by a `deploy/<instance>.N` tag on the repository (README.md, Deployment),
# and once that tag is pushed the git iod reflects it as `git.viff.ref."deploy/<instance>.N"`.
# This rule turns each new one into one message in the channel, through the Slack iod's out half,
# with links to the tag on GitHub: its annotation (what the deploy runs), its tree and its history.
#
# A PACKAGE, SENDING THROUGH AN OUTBOX, as gate-ask.tony is: it writes only inside its own address,
# so the messages land in `out.slack` here, and `sends:` declares that place an outbox of the
# Slack iod's out place. Install it after the Slack iod.
#
# ── THE MESSAGE IS THE LATCH, AND THE SEED ───────────────────────────────────────
#
# A rule selecting on its subject acts on everything already standing when it is installed, so
# without a latch the install announces every deploy there has ever been, and so does every
# reinstall after a wipe. The record in the outbox, keyed by the tag, is that latch, kept in the
# package, which is where a latch belongs: the rule selects a tag no record's `seen` matches,
# `!not.or` over the list, and its own derive writes the `seen` that stops it.
#
# The out half delivers only a record carrying `to`, so a record WITHOUT one is silent, and that
# is the seed: before installing, write `{seen: {name: <tag>}}` into the outbox for every tag the
# remote already has (`viff data announce out slack <tag> --put '{seen: {name: <tag>}}'`).
# Seeding after installing is a race the install wins.
#
# The channel is named by id because the out half takes a Slack id (`C…`) and not a name, and the
# Slack iod's bot has to be in it. Change the id, the workspace in `sends:` and the repository in
# the links for your own.

at: announce
reads: [git.viff.ref]
sends:
- from: out.slack
  to: slack.example.out
strata:
- name: deploy-tags
  level: 0
  match: {path: "git.viff.ref"}
- name: announced
  level: 10
  match: {path: "announce.out.slack"}
rules:
- name: deploy-announce
  stratum: deploy-tags
  condition:
    subject:
      path: "git.viff.ref.*"
      value: !let
        let:
        - seen: !list-paths {at: "announce.out.slack.*", path: seen}
        in: !and
        - {name: !glob "deploy/*"}
        # `.[seen]` is a list: `!list-paths` answers with one, `[{name: <tag>}, …]`, and the
        # let puts it in place before `!or` reads it, so `!or` gets one pattern per record.
        # None matching is a tag not yet announced; an empty list matches none and selects all.
        - !not.or .[seen]
  action:
    derive:
    - path: "announce.out.slack"
      id: .[subject.value.name]
      value:
        to: C0EXAMPLE000
        seen: {name: .[subject.value.name]}
        text: "`$[subject.value.name]` is out: <https://github.com/example/app/releases/tag/$[subject.value.name]|tag> · <https://github.com/example/app/tree/$[subject.value.name]|tree> · <https://github.com/example/app/commits/$[subject.value.name]|history>"
